cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "acqsearch: spatial acquisition search for an optical terminal"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Acharya
    given-names: Om
    affiliation: OPTIMA Organisation
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-16"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OmAcharya-avtr/acqsearch"
abstract: >-
  Research-grade Python library for spatial acquisition search of a free-space
  optical terminal. Computes coverage of an initial pointing-uncertainty
  distribution against dwell index for four scan patterns, expected
  acquisition time analytically and by seeded Monte Carlo with the two
  cross-checked, the optimal dwell time from the detection-probability and
  false-alarm trade, and the probability of acquisition within a declared
  deadline. Includes a Bayesian-greedy adaptive scan-order baseline and a
  learned gradient-boosted scan-order policy with a prediction interval,
  benchmarked against each other and against the fixed patterns on held-out
  scenarios. Not flight-qualified, not certified, not approved for
  operational aerospace use.
keywords:
  - optical communications
  - pointing acquisition tracking
  - spatial acquisition
  - scan pattern
  - search theory
  - aerospace
